    "title": "D4vd Arrested in Connection With Death of Celeste Rivas Hernandez",
    "text": "L.A.P.D. Arrests D4vd Months After Finding Teen’s Remains in His TeslaThe singer was detained in connection with the death of Celeste Rivas Hernandez, who died before her 15th birthday. D4vd’s lawyers said they would vigorously defend his innocence.The body of a teenage girl was found in a car belonging to the singer D4vd. Credit...Jordan Strauss/Invision, via Associated PressApril 16, 2026The musician known as D4vd was arrested on Thursday in connection with the death of a missing teenage girl whose severely decomposed body was found in the trunk of his Tesla, the authorities said.The police did not immediately offer details about their investigation or say what evidence led them to D4vd, whose real name is David Burke. He was arrested in Hollywood around 4:30 p.m., according to Capt. Scot Williams of the Los Angeles Police Department.Online jail records show that Mr. Burke was booked into jail just after 10 p.m.; the records say he is being held without bail and the police have said the case will be presented to prosecutors on Monday.Mr. Burke, 21, has millions of followers on social media and music platforms and created the anthem for Fortnite. His major-label debut, “Withered,” was released last year, and he got an opening slot on SZA’s SOS Tour.In a statement on Thursday, lawyers for Mr. Burke emphasized that he had been detained but not charged with a crime.“The actual evidence in this case will show that David Burke did not murder Celeste Rivas Hernandez and he was not the cause of her death,” said the lawyers, Blair Berk, Marilyn Bednarski and Regina Peter.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.A correction was made onApril 16, 2026: An earlier version of a capsule summary with this article misstated the status of D4vd’s case. He was arrested in connection with a teenage girl’s death but has not been charged with a crime.Matt Stevens is a Times reporter who writes about arts and culture from Los Angeles.Orlando Mayorquín is a Times reporter covering California. He is based in Los Angeles.A version of this article appears in print on April 18, 2026, Section C, Page 6 of the New York edition with the headline: Police Arrest D4vd In Investigation Of a Teen’s Death. Order Reprints | Today’s Paper | SubscribeRelated ContentAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
